    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for gangliocytoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Dominique Figarella-Branger",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 444.85pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Essential:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A tumefactive lesion with presence of irregular groups of large, mature ganglion cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>AND</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Matrix resembling normal neuropil, sometimes more coarsely fibrillar or vacuolated</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>Desirable:</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Atypical and binucleated ganglion cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 444.85pt; background: #EFF6FC; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"593\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cytoplasmic ballooning or vacuolization</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
